From: SB4-Edge-Linux
Subject: [PATCH] main: don't abort when a client vanishes while a client table is gone

client_vanished_cb() asserts that every sensor type has a client table. The tables are freed when the
daemon tears down its sensor data, and a client that disconnects at that moment (or any later name-owner
change) then aborts the daemon with "client_vanished_cb: assertion failed: (ht)", which leaves automatic
brightness off until the next boot. Seen twice on the Galaxy Book4 Edge (light sensor only, through SSC).
Skip sensor types without a table instead.

---
 src/iio-sensor-proxy.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -449,7 +449,8 @@ client_vanished_cb (GDBusConnection *connection,
 		guint watch_id;
 
 		ht = data->clients[i];
-		g_assert (ht);
+		if (ht == NULL)
+			continue;
 
 		watch_id = GPOINTER_TO_UINT (g_hash_table_lookup (ht, sender));
 		if (watch_id > 0)
